#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0460 expect=noViolation domain=AE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the High Level Term (--HLT) is not on the MedDRA primary system organ class hierarchy path.
#note "EC-36 pin, negative twin: every AESOC is genuinely on its AEHLT hierarchy path, so the rule must stay quiet. Guards the resolved dictionary_parent against over-firing — before EC-36 this passed only because the operation always returned null. Child and parent carry the MedDRA preferred case: the flag-less rule compares verbatim against the as-authored hierarchy (D-TA-3 default, Fix #266), and since the C1 data repair that hierarchy is authored in the levels' preferred form."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#dictionaries dummy
dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ type=Num label="Sequence Number"
col AEHLT type=Char label="High Level Term"
col AESOC type=Char label="Primary System Organ Class"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 1 | Headaches NEC | Nervous system disorders
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | 2 | Nausea and vomiting symptoms | Gastrointestinal disorders
---
